  "ingredients": [
    "2 (.25 ounce) envelopes active dry yeast",
    "0.25 cup warm water (105 to 115 degrees)",
    "1.5 cups lukewarm milk",
    "0.5 cup white sugar",
    "1 teaspoon salt",
    "2 eggs",
    "0.33333334326744 cup shortening",
    "5 cups all-purpose flour",
    "1 quart vegetable oil for frying",
    "0.33333334326744 cup butter",
    "2 cups confectioners' sugar",
    "1.5 teaspoons vanilla",
    "4 tablespoons hot water or as needed"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Sprinkle the yeast over the warm water, and let stand for 5 minutes, or until foamy.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/pYm6IOQhlNE8KYX5aoQBlz5N_OI=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/45921-crispy-and-creamy-doughnuts-ddmfs-step-1-517-3x4-cb64ae0ea9724b7d83c42b50b093ad06.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/45921/step_01.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mix yeast mixture, milk, sugar, salt, eggs, shortening, and 2 cups of the flour together in a large bowl for a few minutes with an electric mixer at low speed, or stir with a wooden spoon. Beat in remaining flour, ½ cup at a time, until the dough no longer sticks to the bowl. Knead for about 5 minutes, or until smooth and elastic. Place the dough into a greased bowl, and cover. Set in a warm place to rise until double. Dough is ready if you touch it, and the indention remains.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/s7uIgwmDRem5eqaYRq-a6fdFprQ=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/45921-crispy-and-creamy-doughnuts-ddmfs-step-4-556-3x4-257a3f64736848e28f966792d7dfe033.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/45921/step_02.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Turn the dough out onto a floured surface, and gently roll out to ½-inch thickness. Cut with a floured doughnut cutter. Let doughnuts sit out to rise again until double. Cover loosely with a cloth.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/cBPSZNvizIzy9X_NMIRvvqq6lIQ=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/45921-crispy-and-creamy-doughnuts-ddmfs-step-5-560-3x4-ad8a6d3f24e84ef388a17deca0fc3c8a.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/45921/step_03.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Melt butter in a saucepan over medium heat. Stir in confectioners' sugar and vanilla until smooth. Remove from heat, and stir in hot water one tablespoon at a time until the icing is somewhat thin, but not watery. Set aside.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/GDlTXN_mO8hkkOoETr7-NAsTD-Q=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/45921-crispy-and-creamy-doughnuts-ddmfs-step-6-578-3x4-2612125854f54e379fd8d94dcb87cbd0.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/45921/step_04.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Heat oil in a deep-fryer or large heavy skillet to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C). Slide donuts into the hot oil using a wide spatula. Turn donuts over as they rise to the surface. Fry donuts on each side until golden brown. Remove from hot oil, to drain on a wire rack. Dip donuts into the glaze while still hot, and set onto wire racks to drain off excess. Keep a cookie sheet or tray under racks for easier clean up.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/QatJCVPGkZ5LLnmdemkrh3ZOPc0=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/45921-crispy-and-creamy-doughnuts-ddmfs-step-9-628-3x4-72fe76352bb1473aa2a974db27574820.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/45921/step_05.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Enjoy!",
      "section": null,
